# Short 6, "The Bass page" (vertical, tools/film.py --layout vertical): Night Drive playing (the Growl bass, the
# Sync groove), LFO for the Bass page; Groove through Drone, Offbeat, Dotted, Roller and back to Sync; Octave up
# one; ALGORITHM through the bass voices, Punch, Rubber and Pluck (the octave home), and back to Growl; then
# Fifth up (a slow turn). Every move from a bar's downbeat. Each `bar` prints the film's time there (the cue
# sheet for the labels).
turn PRESET 5 5
wait 30
expect piece 5
bar 8
wav 15-short-bass.wav
film 15-short-bass.film
bar 8 NIGHT DRIVE playing (Bb Dorian, 124)
bar 10 LFO: the Bass page
tap LFO
bar 11 KNOB 3, Groove: Drone
turn K3 -4 150
expect par24 0
bar 13 Groove: Offbeat
turn K3 1 150
bar 14 Groove: Dotted
turn K3 1 150
bar 15 Groove: Roller
turn K3 1 150
bar 17 Groove: back to Sync
turn K3 1 150
expect par24 4
bar 19 KNOB 2, Octave up one
turn K2 1 150
expect par23 1
bar 21 the octave home; ALGORITHM: the voice Punch
turn K2 -1 150
turn ALGO 2 150
expect par23 0
expect par34 1
bar 23 Rubber
turn ALGO 1 300
expect par34 2
bar 25 Pluck
turn ALGO 1 300
expect par34 3
bar 27 back to Growl
turn ALGO 1 300
expect par34 4
bar 28 KNOB 4, Fifth 25 up to 70: the fifth more often
turn K4 45 50
expect par25 70
bar 33 END
filmstop
wavstop
